<title>USA: Clinton wishes Yeltsin a &quot;speedy recovery&quot;.</title>
<headline>Clinton wishes Yeltsin a &quot;speedy recovery&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>SOUIX FALLS, S.D. 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton has sent Russian President Boris Yeltsin &quot;best wishes for a speedy recovery&quot; from his heart operation, White House Press Secretary Mike McCurry said late Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The president has authorised a message to President Yeltsin offering his best wishes for a speedy recovery,&quot; McCurry said.</p>
<p>McCurry's comments came just hours after Yeltsin's surgery began in a Moscow hospital. Clinton was in South Dakota on the last stop of his campaign for re-election.</p>
</text>
